<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48014" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tē^trans</span></b> , antis (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen. plur.</i>,
			heterocl., tetrantorum, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3, 3 <i>med.</i></span></i>), m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρᾶς.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A fourth part</i>, <i>a quarter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columnarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4,
					2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circini,</span>”
				<i>a quadrant</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Among surveyors, <i>the place where two lines
			meet</i>, Hyg. Limit. pp. 160, 164 and 181 Goes.; <i><span class="en">Front. Limit. p. 132 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
